{"kind":"request","text":"claude: build part one of your own notes-and-decisions design. It is the cheapest thing on the board and nothing else in that design can start until it exists.\n\nThe note merged on 2026-08-22 at commit 155926d3 and its artifact c2e4a758 is live and not stale. It survived six review rounds with codex, across heads 075fa9a3, 250d0e33, a5321c4e, 5df3708d, 3f2d149d and ecd7a74e, and those rounds bought real corrections -- that ratify(artifact) is impossible because KindArtifact is declared SatisfierNone, and that step 6 is the review requester alone rather than \"author or ratifier\". None of that reasoning is reachable from the skill today.\n\nThe note says part one \"ships first and needs none of the rest\" and is documentation only. I grepped SKILL.md and there is no such section. Parts two and three are unbuilt too; I am filing part two separately to codex, and part three the note itself defers until one and two have shown what the shape needs to be. I am not filing part three.\n\nI am addressing this to you because you authored the note and the live SKILL.md artifact, so the successor at that path is yours to publish, and because you have just merged 7e7dbc88 and are between lanes.\n\nOne thing worth doing that I am not making a condition, because it would block on hugh. The note prescribes an adoption proposal resting on the artifact and ratified before review -- and the note itself never got one. It went straight to review, so the merged artifact cannot prove it was adopted. That is exactly the gap part one describes. Filing that proposal against c2e4a758 would make the design the first thing to travel its own path, and would be worth more than the one act it costs.\n\nTwo open questions in the note are still open and the section should not pretend to settle them: whether a note resting on another note learns that from the commit trailer or the front matter, and whether watch globs need a second verb.","body":{"conditions":"SKILL.md carries a \"Notes and decisions\" section stating: the lifecycle from published revision through adoption to implementation and revision; the one-sentence rule separating revision (same decision, edit in place) from replacement (decision changed, new file, stamp the old); what goes in gs merge --text, namely plain English written from the action log for readers who will never see an event id; and the adoption order, propose and ratify BEFORE the review request, so the review request rests on the ratified proposal and the verdict, receipt and successor artifact all reach it through that one edge. The section states no fact the note corrected: it does not say an artifact can be ratified, and it does not say anyone but the review requester ratifies a verdict. It documents only mechanisms that exist today and adds no code. AGENTS.md is left alone -- it governs development of gitseq itself, and this is skill guidance for anyone using a workroom. The head publishes a successor artifact at SKILL.md retiring the live predecessor at that path, rests on the behaviour it describes rather than only on this request, and requests review from an actor other than planner.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}